Or... keys only work on some locks and not others. The Dungeons of
Doom have more than one locksmith, although each locksmith left
some of their universal keys behind..

How do you decide what locks the keys work on?  Maybe, when a key is
made, set key->spe = rn2(16), then test the bits:
key->spe & 1 => key fits doors in depths [1,quest]
key->spe & 2 => key fits doors in depths (quest,castle]
key->spe & 4 => key fits doors in depths (castle, ...)
key->spe & 8 => key fits non-door locks

(Assuming spe is unused for keys)

So there's a small chance of getting a key that fits nothing,
and a small chance that a key fits everything, but most of your
keys will fit some stuff but not other stuff. The MKoT fits
everything of course.

